<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
  <!--
    SraiOperators.mml
    Declarative contract for the SRAI operator dispatch surface.

    SRAI performs symbolic redirection through the AIML pattern matcher.
    KHANARY extends this: "XCFE <OP> *" patterns are intercepted by
    aiml_engine and routed to xcfe_executor.cpp as typed dispatch frames.
    This document formalizes the operator set, phase assignments, input/output
    roles, and the authority constraints on each operator.

    Content dictionary: urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1
  -->

  <!-- ── Operator dispatch chain ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>SraiChain</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mi>SCORE</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>RANK</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>COLLAPSE</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>VERIFY</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>TRAIN</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>Xul</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">OperatorChain</csymbol>
        <list>
          <ci>SCORE</ci><ci>RANK</ci><ci>COLLAPSE</ci>
          <ci>VERIFY</ci><ci>TRAIN</ci><ci>Xul</ci>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
SRAI → SCORE → RANK → COLLAPSE → VERIFY → TRAIN → Xul commit.
TRAIN must not run automatically after RANK. A verified_outcome from Ch'en
is a hard prerequisite for any TRAIN dispatch. The chain is a directed pipeline;
no operator can shortcut to Xul without traversing Ch'en verification.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── Operator binding frame ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>BindingFrame</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>operator</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>executor</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>phase</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>inputRoles</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>outputRole</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>effects</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">BindingFrame</csymbol>
        <list><ci>operator</ci><ci>executor</ci><ci>phase</ci>
          <ci>inputRoles</ci><ci>outputRole</ci><ci>effects</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Each XCFE SRAI handler carries a typed binding frame encoding its operator name,
C++ executor target, canonical authority phase, typed input roles, output role,
and declared side-effect set. The frame is the machine contract; the AIML
template text embeds it as [XCFE:OP ...] for aiml_engine interception.
effects must be a subset of {read, measure, order, analyze, gate, project,
emit, collapse, propose_delta}. Operators with effects containing "propose_delta"
additionally require commit_requires fields.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── SCORE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>SCORE</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ctx</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>scored_candidates</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">ScoreOp</csymbol>
        <ci>candidate_set</ci><ci>query_vector</ci><ci>context</ci>
        <ci>scored_candidates</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
SCORE evaluates W·C·R, vector similarity, and metric evidence for each candidate.
Executor: metric (METRIC-µ). Phase: Sek. Effects: read, measure.
Output scored_candidates carries per-candidate score_tau(Q,K | tau,r,F,theta,provider).
SCORE does not select or admit; it populates the evidence field for RANK.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── RANK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>RANK</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>scored</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ctx</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>ranked_candidates</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">RankOp</csymbol>
        <ci>scored_candidates</ci><ci>context</ci><ci>ranked_candidates</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
RANK orders the admitted scored_candidates set. Executor: metric. Phase: Sek.
Effects: read, order. XCFE legality is a separate hard gate; a high rank score
cannot promote an inadmissible candidate. RANK does not commit or authorize.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── COLLAPSE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>COLLAPSE</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>ranked</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>critic</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>collapsed_candidate</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">CollapseOp</csymbol>
        <ci>ranked_candidates</ci><ci>critic_reports</ci><ci>collapsed_candidate</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
COLLAPSE performs total-order reduction via Jyggalag (T=0.00, Ch'en phase).
The Greymarch output record names the surviving candidate; it is not a topology
commit. Xul commit authority still requires the full Proposal → Ch'en → XCFE →
Xul path. The Sheogorath/Jyggalag pair must appear as a unit; Sheogorath
generates the high-entropy set that COLLAPSE reduces.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── VERIFY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>VERIFY</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>candidate</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>evidence</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>verified_outcome</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">VerifyOp</csymbol>
        <ci>candidate</ci><ci>evidence_refs</ci><ci>verified_outcome</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
VERIFY is the Ch'en gate. Executor: ch_en_gate. Authority phase: Ch'en.
verified_outcome is the only input that unlocks TRAIN. Without verified_outcome,
TRAIN dispatch is blocked (XCFE TRAIN UNVERIFIED). VERIFY does not commit;
it produces a gate token that TRAIN and Xul both require.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── TRAIN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>TRAIN</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>verified</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>feedback</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>&#x0394;W</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>Xul</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">TrainOp</csymbol>
        <ci>verified_outcome</ci><ci>verified_feedback</ci>
        <ci>weight_delta</ci><ci>Xul</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
TRAIN proposes W_learned delta from verified feedback. Executor: learning.
Phase: Xul. Requires: verified_outcome (from VERIFY/Ch'en), Xul_authorization.
W_effective = W_corpus * W_learned — only W_learned is updated. W_corpus is
read-only corpus weight; it is never overwritten by a TRAIN delta.
commit_requires: Ch'en_verification AND Xul_authorization. A daemon cannot
recursively redirect itself into uncontrolled training.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── Remaining operators ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>OpSet</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mo>{</mo>
      <mi>COMPARE</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>RECALL</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>PROJECT</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>QUESTION</mi>
      <mo>}</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">SupportingOperators</csymbol>
        <list><ci>COMPARE</ci><ci>RECALL</ci><ci>PROJECT</ci><ci>QUESTION</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
COMPARE(a,b,evidence) → comparison_report. Executor: eliza. Phase: Ch'en. read,analyze.
RECALL(query,phase,ctx) → gram_evidence. Executor: gram_store. Phase: Pop. read.
PROJECT(substrate,ctx,traj_id) → result_substrate. Executor: vector_mu. Phase: Yax. read,project. No mutation.
QUESTION(intent_gap,ctx,history) → question_record. Executor: question_selector. Phase: Yax. read,emit.
All four feed scored_candidates or evidence_refs into the SCORE→RANK pipeline.
None can commit topology; none bypass the Ch'en→Xul authority path.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── W_effective invariant ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <msub><mi>W</mi><mi>effective</mi></msub>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <msub><mi>W</mi><mi>corpus</mi></msub>
      <mo>&#x22C5;</mo>
      <msub><mi>W</mi><mi>learned</mi></msub>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <eq/>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">EffectiveWeight</csymbol></apply>
        <apply>
          <times/>
          <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">CorpusWeight</csymbol></apply>
          <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:srai-operators:v1">LearnedWeight</csymbol></apply>
        </apply>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
W_effective = W_corpus * W_learned.
W_corpus: read-only gram/corpus weight from GramStore; set by the scraper pipeline.
W_learned: mutable weight updated by TRAIN after Ch'en+Xul authorization.
TRAIN targets only W_learned. W_corpus is never overwritten by a learning delta.
This preserves the corpus as a stable baseline while allowing incremental learning.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
SraiOperators contract invariants:
1. SRAI redirects text through the pattern matcher; XCFE dispatch requires the [XCFE:OP] binding frame.
2. Every operator declares phase, executor, input roles, output role, and effects before dispatch.
3. TRAIN requires verified_outcome from Ch'en; raw RANK output alone does not authorize learning.
4. W_effective = W_corpus * W_learned; W_corpus is read-only; TRAIN updates only W_learned.
5. COLLAPSE produces a Greymarch record; it is not a topology commit.
6. No operator can shortcut to Xul without traversing the Ch'en verification gate.
7. This document describes operator contracts; aiml_engine.cpp + xcfe_executor.cpp supply the implementation.
  </annotation>
</math>
